components.responsibility:
Covers every material case in the matrix that touches Scanner, DirectoryReader or the report, each on a real NTFS tree under %TEMP% with an injected fake store:
- root above the store;
- root at the store;
- siblings Layers2, 'Layers.' and 'Layers ' (created via \\?\);
- subst root and \\?\Volume{GUID}\ root;
- root spelled in a different case;
- a store beyond MAX_PATH;
- the backstop called directly;
- no store present;
- report members.
The existing counting-rule tests (links, hardlinks, on-disk size, long paths, unreadable folders) run unchanged and must still pass, since this slice touches the scanner.

Runs the published exe on C:\ProgramData\Microsoft\Windows\Containers with --report. Asserts:
- exactly one skippedStores entry, for Layers;
- opensUnderExcludedStore = 0;
- an unreadable count that does not include the store.
If no store exists, it reports SKIPPED with the reason, never a pass.

Adds whatever the protocol needs that the hook does not already do:
- start a scan of a given root;
- Cancel or close at a folder count (FSA_HOOK_AT_FOLDERS);
- close after the scan finishes;
- on scan end or cancel, write a line to FSA_HOOK_LOG and wait FSA_HOOK_HOLD_S before closing, so the 'done, process alive' mark can be taken.
Existing FSA_HOOK_MODE names (stop|throw|close) are kept.

key_decisions.decision:
One true Restart, then a person-run protocol in a fixed order, with no build after the restart.
Before the restart:
- build the fixed publish, the afd021d publish and ScanArm;
- check the hook on %TEMP%;
- paste the fltmc output;
- take the pre-restart mark.
After the restart, in order:
- the post-restart mark and a 10-minute idle baseline (B0);
- L: ScanArm listing-only over all of C:;
- P: PlainOpen over half H2's files;
- F1-F5: fixed app, completed;
- X1-X5: fixed app, cancelled (3 Cancel, 2 close, target = skippedAtFolderCount + 1,000);
- the pressure step;
- U1: afd021d cancelled at skippedAtFolderCount + 1,000, which lands mid-layer;
- U2: afd021d completed;
- U3: afd021d completed again;
- `dir /a /s <Layers>`, then `dir /a /s /b C:\` twice.

proposals.note:
The only proposal. Taken as the core, with six changes:
- default store list moved from ScanOptions.cs into ContainerLayerStore;
- fitness patterns rewritten to the (?m) prefix that rules-parity requires;
- the PoolWatch 'no fltmc' rule dropped, because its literal pattern fires on the correct paste prompt;
- a rule added that keeps OpenDirectory at one call site, which the backstop depends on;
- a rule added that keeps ProbeRule assignments out of src;
- the U arms reordered (cancelled first) so the unfixed cancelled run can show anything.
